Task: histogram
Given a string representing space separated lowercase letters, return a dictionary of the letter with the most repetition and containing the corresponding count. If several letters have the same occurrence, return all of them. (A dictionary is a list of key-value pairs here, in any order.)

Definitions (Lean):
@[reducible, simp]
def histogram_precond (test : String) : Prop :=
  True

@[reducible, simp]
def histogram_postcond (test : String) (result: List (String × Nat)) (h_precond : histogram_precond (test)) :=
  let ws := (test.splitOn " ").filter (fun w => w != "")
  (ws = [] → result = []) ∧
  (ws ≠ [] → (∀ p ∈ result, p.1 ∈ ws ∧ p.2 = ws.count p.1 ∧ ∀ w ∈ ws, ws.count w ≤ p.2) ∧
    (∀ w ∈ ws, (∀ v ∈ ws, ws.count v ≤ ws.count w) → ∃ p ∈ result, p.1 = w) ∧ (result.map Prod.fst).Nodup)

Goal 1: find ρ : List (String × Nat)
test : String
h_precond : histogram_precond test
⊢ ∃ ρ, histogram_postcond test ρ h_precond

